# ESP32 Soil Moisture Monitoring System Using FreeRTOS
This project is designed to learn "Embedded Systems and FreeRTOS" using an ESP32 and a soil moisture sensor. The system periodically reads soil sensor values, displays the readings on the Serial Monitor, and activates a buzzer when the soil condition crosses a predefined threshold.
The project uses FreeRTOS multitasking to separate the system into three independent tasks: "Sensor Task", "Display Task", and "Alert Task". Queues are used for communication between tasks, while task priorities and delays demonstrate real-time scheduling and efficient CPU utilization. Hysteresis-based threshold control helps prevent frequent buzzer switching near the alarm limits.
This project provides practical experience with sensor interfacing, GPIO control, task creation, task priorities, inter-task communication, queues, and real-time operating system concepts using ESP32 and Arduino.
# code:
#include <Arduino.h>
#define SOIL_PIN 34
#define BUZZER_PIN 26

struct SensorData {
    int soilValue;
    int dryThreshold;
};
QueueHandle_t displayQueue;
QueueHandle_t alertQueue;
void sensorTask(void *p) {
  SensorData d;
    while (true) {
        d.soilValue = analogRead(SOIL_PIN);
        d.dryThreshold = 2700;
        if (!isnan(d.soilValue) &&
            !isnan(d.dryThreshold)) {
            xQueueOverwrite(displayQueue, &d);
            xQueueOverwrite(alertQueue, &d);
        }
        vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(2000));
    }
}
void displayTask(void *p) {
    SensorData d;
    while (true) {
        if (xQueueReceive(displayQueue,  &d, portMAX_DELAY) == pdTRUE) {
            Serial.print("Soil Value: ");
            Serial.println(d.soilValue);
        }
    }
}

void alertTask(void *p) {
    SensorData d;
    bool alarm = false;

    while (true) {
        if (xQueueReceive( alertQueue, &d,portMAX_DELAY) == pdTRUE) {
   if (d.soilValue >4000)
      alarm = true;
     if (d.soilValue < 3000)
     alarm = false;
       digitalWrite( BUZZER_PIN,  alarm ? HIGH : LOW);
   }
 }
}

void setup() {
    Serial.begin(115200);
    pinMode(BUZZER_PIN, OUTPUT);
    digitalWrite(BUZZER_PIN, LOW);
    displayQueue = xQueueCreate(1, sizeof(SensorData));
    alertQueue = xQueueCreate(1, sizeof(SensorData));
    xTaskCreate(
        sensorTask, "Sensor",4096, NULL, 3, NULL);
    xTaskCreate(
      displayTask, "Display",3072, NULL, 1, NULL);
    xTaskCreate(
   alertTask, "Alert",3072, NULL, 2, NULL);
}
void loop() {
    vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(1000));
}
